      "observed": "U4 pin 28 (VCC, power_in) is only connected to C7 pin 1; C7 pin 2 is on GND. The global VCC net includes U4 pin 6 (VBAT), pin 9 (VDD), and pin 11 (BS1), but not U4 pin 28.",
      "expected": "The SSD1306 VCC supply pin should be connected to the board VCC supply (or the appropriate analog supply) and then decoupled to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"17\") (name \"Net-(U4-VCC)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"28\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"VCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "`C7` (2.2 µF) — U4 `VCC` (digital-logic supply pin) to GND"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED controller's VCC supply input would be floating/unpowered, likely preventing the display from initializing or producing visible output.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows the SSD1306 VCC power_in pin connected only to a decoupling capacitor to GND and not to the board VCC rail, which is a likely missing supply connection for the display."
}

